;; CLean — R3 (predictive-coding belief update) decomposed into its sub-boxes, with the UNBUILT
;; sign-aggregation box marked as a typed hole. The ◐→box-pointer: this replaces "R3 is partial"
;; with "R3 needs the :sign-aggregation box (designed-dark, approved, not wired)."
;; clean_argcheck-valid; build-match-checkable.

{:clean/proof "R3-decomposition"
 :clean/title "R3: prediction error + precision + VFE + belief update — which box remains"
 :clean/source {:requirement "R3" :status "FILLED — 8 channels + sign-aggregation + per-entity attribution all built/live; only fine per-channel attribution (research-level, partly infeasible) remains" :commit "3347575+ced3aec+v0.17-attribution"}

 :clean/seq [:per-channel-errors :precision-weighting :vfe-decomposition :sign-aggregation :belief-update]

 :clean/boxes
 [{:id :b1 :method :per-channel-errors
   :text "R3a: prediction error per observation channel. 8 of 14 channels have likelihood models (predict-* functions producing {:mean :variance}). compute-prediction-error returns {:observed :predicted-mean :error} per channel. Built, validated on real runs (2026-05-18: +0.37/−0.15/−0.24/−0.20)."
   :produces :per-channel-errors}
  {:id :b2 :method :precision-weighting
   :text "R3b: precision Π = 1/max(variance, ε) with ε = 0.01. weighted-error = error × Π. Applied per channel at the prediction-error step. Built for all 8 covered channels."
   :consumes [:per-channel-errors]
   :produces :precision-weighted-errors}
  {:id :b3 :method :vfe-decomposition
   :text "R3c: variational free energy decomposed into pragmatic + epistemic + per-channel detail. compute-free-energy reports G per tick. In shape since v0.2."
   :consumes [:precision-weighted-errors]
   :produces :variational-free-energy}
  {:id :b4 :method :sign-aggregation
   :text "R3d (the hard half): combine the 8 precision-weighted errors into one R3d driver. channel-health-signs for all 8 channels; r3d-aggregate-driver uses the precision-weighted average: Sigma(sign_c · precision_c · error_c) / Sigma(precision_c). BUILT + ARMED behind *r3d-multichannel?* (default ON as of b624242, Joe-directed; bind false to restore annotation-health-alone byte-identical). Tier-1, world-inert, latent until R10."
   :produces :aggregated-r3d-driver}
  {:id :b5 :method :belief-update
   :text "R3d belief-update, per-entity. BUILT + LIVE (war_machine.clj:3806-3833, v0.17 sorry/r3d-per-entity-attribution): the aggregated R3d driver is distributed ACROSS entities weighted by each entity's inconsistency with the error direction (1-h when healthier-than-predicted, h when unhealthier), normalised so the mean equals the event-weight — aggregate magnitude preserved, attribution honest (not uniform, not flag-gated). Discharges the R3 want-signature. RESEARCH REMAINDER (not a clean build): FINE per-channel per-entity attribution — routing each channel's error to the entities that channel concerns — is only feasible for the per-entity channels (annotation/support/attack-coverage, active-repo-ratio); the graph-global channels (coupling-density, mission-health, ticks-firing-ratio) have no per-entity decomposition. Today's attribution uses the annotation-health expected-health as a single-channel proxy for the whole aggregate."
   :consumes [:variational-free-energy :aggregated-r3d-driver]
   :produces :updated-belief-state
   :discharges {:to :predictive-coding-belief-update}}]

 :clean/wires
 [{:from :b1 :to :b2 :carries :per-channel-errors}
  {:from :b2 :to :b3 :carries :precision-weighted-errors}
  {:from :b3 :to :b5 :carries :variational-free-energy}
  {:from :b4 :to :b5 :carries :aggregated-r3d-driver}]

 :clean/copar [{:reading :informal :is :clean/seq}
               {:reading :formal   :is [:clean/boxes :clean/wires]}]

 :clean/shape {:macro :predictive-coding-with-sign-aggregation
               :holes-at []
               :discharges-at [:b5]
               :note "b1 (per-channel-errors) ✓, b2 (precision-weighting) ✓, b3 (VFE) ✓, b4 (sign-aggregation) ✓ (BUILT behind *r3d-multichannel?*, precision-weighted average), b5 (belief-update) ✓ — per-entity attribution is BUILT + LIVE (war_machine.clj:3806-3833, v0.17): the aggregate is distributed by per-entity inconsistency, not uniformly. ZERO unbuilt boxes. The only remainder is RESEARCH-level: fine per-channel per-entity attribution (partly infeasible — graph-global channels have no per-entity decomposition), tracked on b5."}}
